.TH "CLOSEWATCHER.DESTROY" "3JS" "March 2, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CloseWatcher.destroy \- CloseWatcher: destroy() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]destroy()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]CloseWatcher\f[R]
interface deactivates the close watcher.
This is intended to be called if the relevant UI element is torn down in
some other way than being closed.
.PP
After being deactivated, this \f[CR]CloseWatcher\f[R] will no longer
receive \f[CR]cancel\f[R] or \f[CR]close\f[R] events, and it will be
possible to create new independent \f[CR]CloseWatcher\f[R] instances.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
destroy()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using the \f[CR]destroy()\f[R] method
Use the \f[CR]destroy()\f[R] method to dispose of the watcher instance
for cleanup.
.IP
.EX
watcher.destroy();
.EE
